odhya","sarga":48,"verse":19,"english":"O Kākutstha, I behold you come after a long time. I have heard of your causeless exile.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.569,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ac4417e89695738368817379b54cf8c4d7d041f4829ab52c248de71ac2c874f","compact":"7c9e17418b7caa8837dd59c956515358431f5818ea4438762e7a2b6f4e6ce31e","nasal":"7c9e17418b7caa8837dd59c956515358431f5818ea4438762e7a2b6f4e6ce31e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":20,"english":"This spot at the meeting of the mighty rivers is lonely, sacred and charming. Do you dwell here happily.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fac1f65ddd466312c0422a3b959ecf2ae75c7af7c6e589333c181e8e94e9616a","compact":"db147f895ebe4a94dcb88312f2412d8369f5e0f8fe7fec878225b6ad3119d211","nasal":"db147f895ebe4a94dcb88312f2412d8369f5e0f8fe7fec878225b6ad3119d211"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":21,"english":"Thus addressed by Bharadvāja, that descendant of Raghu, Rāma intent on the welfare of all, answered in auspicious words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f80ec6b0e9303a6e21513af8a0b7dc4991c8eb47bae9d99bf25ad16f9938f3fc","compact":"cd462a1eac1ab20b0a59ee462a03d15310c02c2c36b9ea9d2c794b6a8ca4cccf","nasal":"cd462a1eac1ab20b0a59ee462a03d15310c02c2c36b9ea9d2c794b6a8ca4cccf"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":22,"english":"O reverend one, I apprehend that, living hard by, the inhabitants of the city and the provinces, thinking me as easily to be seen, will come to this asylum desirous of beholding me and Vaidehī. It is for this reason that living at this place does not recommended itself to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.835,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21702746a7e5b6e64295d2023ff2303a2eedffd8fd70c9fadbcb9dcad4fffb35","compact":"0e7bc26db2121e0243483c7980e32e03cf6d5ecb1d568bca34556f695246743f","nasal":"2d92ab9bc5fd87fdd251226243cdde5bc5371e52cb1fc3cac6eee23dc6789bb9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":23,"english":"Do you, O worshipful one, hit upon a retired and agreeable asylum where Janaka's daughter worthy of happiness, will pass her days pleasantly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fefec8ef85977cde3752663276957d0c50e7960d37d426bfc676a47812e53842","compact":"692ab1e6715c4a18dbc17c1871e11011e0f47964cbfae015cd4acca722341440","nasal":"6a304b88f1c4245dfcd58f4f60fca50586594b62dfb348faadfdde553c6c90f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":24,"english":"Hearing this auspicious speech of Rāghava, that eminent anchoret Bharadvāja said these words calculated to serve Rāma's purpose.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskr