, one reaps welfare, and ignorance does not envelope one's mind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e909e2c20fb838914d6cedb88cdc2c7d82fca5baf8460ec1cf878f7bd3f73a0","compact":"c56cc3eae3272bbb089291ef6b636368ecc974c999d50255382414f9ffda002c","nasal":"0543e067451505e8b4276d6546dd4d1f28b269460b53c2ae09e12d22c7c2da91"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":28,"english":"There innumerable saints with the hair of their heads rendered white like skulls, having spent hundreds of years, have through austerities ascended heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89b97d4e8ec701aa11a06d272459873d7d04c62b35301ac3f4a30a5c5acf1229","compact":"1b97569e2fa8f4c7a35695c4a23ae032225c581f4744ccdc5a4e4b0df15093de","nasal":"1b97569e2fa8f4c7a35695c4a23ae032225c581f4744ccdc5a4e4b0df15093de"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":29,"english":"That solitary spot I deem as one which will make a happy residence for you. O Rāma, do you, for living out the term of your banishment, dwell either here or with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34366d6e2a2064cfa43d827248fbdb6cb88a623091270f85f2fe9f4cd8513f9f","compact":"d05e17d48508f8f53d04f4907c3d4c2e16dfb5c9fda7522c8afe5b0a7f872f2f","nasal":"d05e17d48508f8f53d04f4907c3d4c2e16dfb5c9fda7522c8afe5b0a7f872f2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":30,"english":"Bharadvāja entertained his welcome guest, Rāma, along with his wife and brother by extending towards them every rite of hospitality.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f519c7641ee5ab0f80b638a32d783a96f7a55d1b091b20b198f7c644db72213c","compact":"2ce9fbe75cd8b061963d1db76e677cccec722bc08fdcd5c9d95f43269ed0bcd2","nasal":"2ce9fbe75cd8b061963d1db76e677cccec722bc08fdcd5c9d95f43269ed0bcd2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":31,"english":"At Prayāga Rāma having obtained the company of that Maharși, and discoursing on a variety of sacred topics, the night came on.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.917,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c404458d6c06ee18ae6e3b7a49b238967eefd421f62df8a12374bf4f388ea205","compact":"a1d2d408c74cb4b6bc834ba4f18f9719ff3d1cb16f6572fe37db1ee790a9cb2b","nasal":"b9408b183e5ec3e499ba704fc3459962e202946bdb59c5cde6a898c87b4df80f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":32,"english":"When the night had passed away and day dawned, (Rāma) approached Bharadvāja, and that chief of men addressed that ascetic of flaming energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"439fe49503027fd3987fbf175f88d3895f65ce4c68828944727620852040bf4c","compact":"2d035dc2618d4ef754fbc78a4fdaffbe1ec16caf03063093434b71dfa9553108","nasal":"2d035dc2618d4ef754fbc78a4fdaffbe1ec16caf03063093434b71dfa9553108"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":33,"english":"O reverend sire of truthful character, we have here in your asylum spent the night. Do you now permit us to set forward (for Citrakuta).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"944ff6edf0a66fce7506cb775fa6292e3fd2e8fba729216cc2e2ef0684669808","compact":"b4ac6ffa779c18d7dd2ef0a3f0ab28c74f04976b06ab4499580cb7afd5e510fe","nasal":"d78dc29931c49f6f702ffb9f3cab0526680cea41609f379b1589a38b8324d137"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":34,"english":"On Rāma having passed the night there, Bharadvāja spoke to him, “Do you race your steps to Citrakuța filled with delicious fruits and roots. I deem that, О mighty Rāma, as a fit abode for you, being, as it is, furnished with various kinds of trees, inhabited by crowds of Kinnars, resounding with the cries of peacocks, and frequented by gigantic elephants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"602787d2e126c73f98752b17b9f5e0d3e53d302c306d1d3fba8e4471c954b518","compact":"12f8d9a45ffd0fce4f79a7266066a15bbb7b7eb19c915c11cf976e99f83cc147","nasal":"dd94d091cc52c5e628ecfa3f6816cbe072ad8e953b38b2192e9e92ffeacad77b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":35,"english":"Do you repair to the famed Citrakuţa, holy, fair to the view, and abounding in countless fruits and roots. And in those forests range herds of elephants and deer; and these, O Rāghava, you will behold. And ranging with Sītā rivers and rills and plateau's, caverns and fountains, your mind will experience delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"357a061f7bd26fc6057d1b16a6f403c152fe52dc87ce322b7a32b116e9840299","compact":"a8d373792ad24e07819b8f57ebcb84b6f6550d776f953a33fb99af54053a3c49","nasal":"43ced4403717b81d75057aa25c5a3651500563d148cb7fde6e9a466c62a5cede"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-48-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":48,"verse":36,"english":"Delighted with the notes of joyous Koyastivas and coels, and the cries of deer and coundess mad elephants, do you, arriving at the auspicious mountain, reside at the romantic asylum.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.525,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-54-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2048036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b34d6ee4cc20e1c1eef3ee9ab2ad83882305ce777ae706161744e7a07fc7d51","compact":"1c0b39ab45d75e8bf36f2d214b1d24ff425c692b6735adb40f13c13742aa448a","nasal":"d9fa123fb937f2c9d76e43c320339239e0b199e9a54feddb2fe2e26cd62433b4"}}]
